    {TEXT("阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("The Arras offensive continued until sixteen May."), TEXT("The Arras offensive continued until sixteen May.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 一九一七年五月三日\n\n铁丝间留着四月战斗的残骸，新的进攻队又来到缺口前。白垩壕肩后冒出枪口，掩蔽部的出口还通着，投弹兵把枪榴弹送向壕角。\n\n前队已经越过障碍，携弹手的箱子却挂住了断丝。后面的人伏下帮他松开，邻段的射击忽近忽远。军士从弹坑里探头，寻找刚才出发的那一班。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · Three May nineteen seventeen\n\nWreckage from April lies in the wire. Another assault party reaches the gap. A muzzle appears over the chalk parapet; the dugout exits are open. Rifle grenades fall towards the traverse while the leading men cross the obstacles.\n\nA bearer's box catches on a strand behind them. The next man lies down to free it. Firing rises and falls on the neighbouring sector. From a shell hole, the NCO searches for the section that has just gone forward.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("一九一七年五月三日，澳大利亚与英国部队再次进攻布勒库尔。四月战斗的残骸仍散在兴登堡线铁丝之间。障碍后，德军纵深壕和掩蔽部仍与后方连通，守军能在炮击之后重返胸墙。\n\n本连接近这片受损障碍，枪榴弹落向壕角，步兵从铁丝缺口向前。英军携弹队随后赶来，前沿壕沟的争夺影响着补给能否抵达已经越过障碍的人员。白垩壕肩与弹坑遮住部分动静，邻队的推进并不同时。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 一九一七年五月三日\n\n铁丝间留着四月战斗的残骸，新的进攻队又来到缺口前。白垩壕肩后冒出枪口，掩蔽部的出口还通着，投弹兵把枪榴弹送向壕角。\n\n前队已经越过障碍，携弹手的箱子却挂住了断丝。后面的人伏下帮他松开，邻段的射击忽近忽远。军士从弹坑里探头，寻找刚才出发的那一班。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · Three May nineteen seventeen\n\nWreckage from April lies in the wire. Another assault party reaches the gap. A muzzle appears over the chalk parapet; the dugout exits are open. Rifle grenades fall towards the traverse while the leading men cross the obstacles.\n\nA bearer's box catches on a strand behind them. The next man lies down to free it. Firing rises and falls on the neighbouring sector. From a shell hole, the NCO searches for the section that has just gone forward.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("On 3 May 1917, Australian and British troops renew the attack at Bullecourt. The April fighting has left wreckage among the Hindenburg Line's wire. Beyond it, deep German trenches and shelters remain connected to the rear, allowing defenders to return to the parapets after bombardment.\n\nThe company is approaching this damaged belt of obstacles. Rifle grenades reach the trench corners while infantry work through gaps in the wire. Ammunition bearers follow from the British side. The fighting around the forward trenches determines whether those carrying supplies can reach the men already beyond the obstacles.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 一九一七年五月三日"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · Three May nineteen seventeen"), TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 一九一七年五月三日")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 一九一七年五月三日"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · Three May nineteen seventeen"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · Three May nineteen seventeen")},
    {TEXT("铁丝间留着四月战斗的残骸，新的进攻队又来到缺口前。白垩壕肩后冒出枪口，掩蔽部的出口还通着，投弹兵把枪榴弹送向壕角。"), TEXT("Wreckage from April lies in the wire. Another assault party reaches the gap. A muzzle appears over the chalk parapet; the dugout exits are open. Rifle grenades fall towards the traverse while the leading men cross the obstacles."), TEXT("铁丝间留着四月战斗的残骸，新的进攻队又来到缺口前。白垩壕肩后冒出枪口，掩蔽部的出口还通着，投弹兵把枪榴弹送向壕角。")},
    {TEXT("铁丝间留着四月战斗的残骸，新的进攻队又来到缺口前。白垩壕肩后冒出枪口，掩蔽部的出口还通着，投弹兵把枪榴弹送向壕角。"), TEXT("Wreckage from April lies in the wire. Another assault party reaches the gap. A muzzle appears over the chalk parapet; the dugout exits are open. Rifle grenades fall towards the traverse while the leading men cross the obstacles."), TEXT("Wreckage from April lies in the wire. Another assault party reaches the gap. A muzzle appears over the chalk parapet; the dugout exits are open. Rifle grenades fall towards the traverse while the leading men cross the obstacles.")},
    {TEXT("前队已经越过障碍，携弹手的箱子却挂住了断丝。后面的人伏下帮他松开，邻段的射击忽近忽远。军士从弹坑里探头，寻找刚才出发的那一班。"), TEXT("A bearer's box catches on a strand behind them. The next man lies down to free it. Firing rises and falls on the neighbouring sector. From a shell hole, the NCO searches for the section that has just gone forward."), TEXT("前队已经越过障碍，携弹手的箱子却挂住了断丝。后面的人伏下帮他松开，邻段的射击忽近忽远。军士从弹坑里探头，寻找刚才出发的那一班。")},
    {TEXT("前队已经越过障碍，携弹手的箱子却挂住了断丝。后面的人伏下帮他松开，邻段的射击忽近忽远。军士从弹坑里探头，寻找刚才出发的那一班。"), TEXT("A bearer's box catches on a strand behind them. The next man lies down to free it. Firing rises and falls on the neighbouring sector. From a shell hole, the NCO searches for the section that has just gone forward."), TEXT("A bearer's box catches on a strand behind them. The next man lies down to free it. Firing rises and falls on the neighbouring sector. From a shell hole, the NCO searches for the section that has just gone forward.")},
    {TEXT("澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("Australian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。")},
    {TEXT("澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("Australian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("Australian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 一九一七年六月七日\n\n地面猛然抬起，山脊的旧壕道没入烟尘。普卢默的第二集团军向前推进，澳新部队在邻段出发。军士循着刚露出的坑岸，寻找通往高处的路。\n\n枪组把枪架拖过松土，携弹手试着踩出一条硬路。原先标定的地形已经改变，担架队在后面停住，等前队报回尚能通行的缺口。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · Seven June nineteen seventeen\n\nThe ground rises and the old ridge trenches vanish into dust. Plumer's Second Army advances; Australian and New Zealand troops move on the adjoining sectors. The NCO follows the fresh crater lip, looking for a passage onto the heights.\n\nThe gun crew drags its mounting over loose earth. A bearer tests each step for firm ground. The landmarks on the sketch have gone. Behind them, the stretcher party waits for word of a gap that will carry a loaded stretcher.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack."), TEXT("一九一七年六月七日破晓前，梅西讷山脊下的地雷爆炸。普卢默的第二集团军按炮兵计划进攻，澳大利亚与新西兰部队也在邻段行动。爆破摧毁壕沟，在接近路上留下陡峭坑岸。\n\n本连随炮火进入破碎地面，步枪手穿行弹坑之间，机枪组把器材带向坑岸。瓦砾中仍有幸存德军哨位，携弹队和担架队从后方跟进。作战准备时标明的小路已有变化，松土和断坡限制部队之间的观察。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 一九一七年六月七日\n\n地面猛然抬起，山脊的旧壕道没入烟尘。普卢默的第二集团军向前推进，澳新部队在邻段出发。军士循着刚露出的坑岸，寻找通往高处的路。\n\n枪组把枪架拖过松土，携弹手试着踩出一条硬路。原先标定的地形已经改变，担架队在后面停住，等前队报回尚能通行的缺口。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · Seven June nineteen seventeen\n\nThe ground rises and the old ridge trenches vanish into dust. Plumer's Second Army advances; Australian and New Zealand troops move on the adjoining sectors. The NCO follows the fresh crater lip, looking for a passage onto the heights.\n\nThe gun crew drags its mounting over loose earth. A bearer tests each step for firm ground. The landmarks on the sketch have gone. Behind them, the stretcher party waits for word of a gap that will carry a loaded stretcher.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack."), TEXT("Before dawn on 7 June 1917, mines explode beneath the German positions on Messines ridge. Plumer's Second Army attacks under a prepared artillery plan, with Australian and New Zealand formations on adjoining sectors. The explosions have destroyed trenches and left steep crater banks across the approaches.\n\nThe company advances into this broken ground behind the bombardment. Riflemen pass between craters while machine gun crews bring their equipment towards the banks. Surviving German posts remain among the debris. Ammunition and stretcher parties follow through passages that have changed since the attack was prepared.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 一九一七年六月七日\n\n地面猛然抬起，山脊的旧壕道没入烟尘。普卢默的第二集团军向前推进，澳新部队在邻段出发。军士循着刚露出的坑岸，寻找通往高处的路。\n\n枪组把枪架拖过松土，携弹手试着踩出一条硬路。原先标定的地形已经改变，担架队在后面停住，等前队报回尚能通行的缺口。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · Seven June nineteen seventeen\n\nThe ground rises and the old ridge trenches vanish into dust. Plumer's Second Army advances; Australian and New Zealand troops move on the adjoining sectors. The NCO follows the fresh crater lip, looking for a passage onto the heights.\n\nThe gun crew drags its mounting over loose earth. A bearer tests each step for firm ground. The landmarks on the sketch have gone. Behind them, the stretcher party waits for word of a gap that will carry a loaded stretcher.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · Seven June nineteen seventeen\n\nThe ground rises and the old ridge trenches vanish into dust. Plumer’s Second Army advances; Australian and New Zealand troops move on the adjoining sectors. The NCO follows the fresh crater lip, looking for a passage onto the heights.\n\nThe gun crew drags its mounting over loose earth. A bearer tests each step for firm ground. The landmarks on the sketch have gone. Behind them, the stretcher party waits for word of a gap that will carry a loaded stretcher.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack.")},
