    {TEXT("梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("British forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("British forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 一九一七年七月三十一日\n\n木板路在积水中断开，前队停在最后一块木板上。城外的排水沟已经被炮火打坏，弹坑连成水面。远处德军枪位开火，水上浮着新溅起的泥。\n\n壕炮组带着器材赶来，野炮还堵在后面的路上。携弹手把箱子举过水面，伤员坐在路边等待。军士试过脚下的硬地，才让下一人跨出。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Pilckem · Thirty-one July nineteen seventeen\n\nThe duckboards end in standing water. The leading men stop on the last plank. Shellfire has broken the drains outside the town and joined the craters into pools. A German gun opens beyond them; fresh mud splashes onto the surface.\n\nThe mortar crew brings its equipment forward. Field guns are caught on the road behind. Bearers lift their boxes above the water, passing wounded men seated beside the path. The NCO tests the ground before the next man steps off.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on thirty-one July."), TEXT("一九一七年七月三十一日，第三次伊普尔战役的皮尔克姆进攻展开。炮火破坏城外排水系统，雨水漫进田野和旧弹坑，德军哨位仍散在积水接近地段。少数干路承载着前线交通。\n\n本连沿尚存硬地和木板路行动。壕炮已经赶到前沿，野炮与补给仍受后方道路阻碍。携弹队和伤员共用少数通路，积水与受损壕沟分开前进部队，也限制着对邻军和德军枪位的观察。炮击还在不断改变道路状况。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 一九一七年七月三十一日\n\n木板路在积水中断开，前队停在最后一块木板上。城外的排水沟已经被炮火打坏，弹坑连成水面。远处德军枪位开火，水上浮着新溅起的泥。\n\n壕炮组带着器材赶来，野炮还堵在后面的路上。携弹手把箱子举过水面，伤员坐在路边等待。军士试过脚下的硬地，才让下一人跨出。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Pilckem · Thirty-one July nineteen seventeen\n\nThe duckboards end in standing water. The leading men stop on the last plank. Shellfire has broken the drains outside the town and joined the craters into pools. A German gun opens beyond them; fresh mud splashes onto the surface.\n\nThe mortar crew brings its equipment forward. Field guns are caught on the road behind. Bearers lift their boxes above the water, passing wounded men seated beside the path. The NCO tests the ground before the next man steps off.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on thirty-one July."), TEXT("The attack towards Pilckem opens on 31 July 1917 as part of the Third Battle of Ypres. Shellfire has damaged the drainage around the city, and rain is filling fields and old craters. German posts remain scattered across the flooded approaches.\n\nThe company's sector follows the surviving firm ground and duckboard paths. Trench mortars have come forward while field batteries and supplies struggle on the roads behind. Ammunition bearers and wounded men share the few usable passages. Water and damaged trenches separate the advancing parties, limiting observation of neighbouring positions and the surviving German guns.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 一九一七年七月三十一日"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Pilckem · Thirty-one July nineteen seventeen"), TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 一九一七年七月三十一日")},
