    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 一九一七年十一月三十日\n\n林口的机枪转了方向，弹带横过刚堆好的土袋。德军反击正在逼近，换防人员和携弹队还往林中走。撤下来的伤员在路口迎面遇见他们。\n\n断树后传来步枪声，浅洼遮住侧翼的动静。军士把返回的人引进交通壕，再让前送的队伍通过。担架的木柄擦过壕壁，刮下一层湿土。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bourlon Wood · Thirty November nineteen seventeen\n\nThe gun at the woodland exit changes direction. Its belt crosses newly stacked sandbags. German counterattacks are closing in while reliefs and ammunition parties still enter the wood. Wounded men meet them at the junction.\n\nRifle fire comes from behind broken trees. A hollow conceals the flank. The NCO guides returning men into the communication trench, then lets the carrying party through. A stretcher handle scrapes wet earth from the wall; the bearers turn it carefully at the bend.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("一九一七年十一月三十日，德军反击压向康布雷附近的英军突出部。布尔隆林旁道路仍前送弹药与换防人员，伤员和撤回部队则向后行进。新的德军接近方向威胁此前位于英军后方的通路。\n\n本连位于林缘出口及其交通壕附近，机枪转向反击方向，照看拥挤道路。断树和浅洼藏着侧翼移动，出口沿线的步兵战斗影响着突出部撤出人员的通行。前行与返回队伍仍在使用同一批狭窄路线。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 一九一七年十一月三十日\n\n林口的机枪转了方向，弹带横过刚堆好的土袋。德军反击正在逼近，换防人员和携弹队还往林中走。撤下来的伤员在路口迎面遇见他们。\n\n断树后传来步枪声，浅洼遮住侧翼的动静。军士把返回的人引进交通壕，再让前送的队伍通过。担架的木柄擦过壕壁，刮下一层湿土。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bourlon Wood · Thirty November nineteen seventeen\n\nThe gun at the woodland exit changes direction. Its belt crosses newly stacked sandbags. German counterattacks are closing in while reliefs and ammunition parties still enter the wood. Wounded men meet them at the junction.\n\nRifle fire comes from behind broken trees. A hollow conceals the flank. The NCO guides returning men into the communication trench, then lets the carrying party through. A stretcher handle scrapes wet earth from the wall; the bearers turn it carefully at the bend.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("German counterattacks on 30 November 1917 are pressing the British salient near Cambrai. At Bourlon Wood, roads carry ammunition and reliefs towards the front while wounded and withdrawing parties move back. New German approaches threaten routes that lay behind the earlier British advance.\n\nThe company is positioned near the woodland exit and its communication trenches. Machine guns are turning towards the counterattack, covering roads crowded with traffic. Broken trees and shallow hollows conceal movement on the flanks. Infantry fighting along the exit affects the passage of troops still coming out of the salient.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 一九一七年十一月三十日"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bourlon Wood · Thirty November nineteen seventeen"), TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 一九一七年十一月三十日")},
