    {TEXT("德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("The German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("The German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 一九一八年二月\n\n哨位没有回答，值更军士又听了一会儿。铁丝前的低地留着脚印，零星枪声从德军阵地方向传来。轻装巡逻队走进湿沟，后面的人掩住灯光。\n\n前哨与连部之间有几段断线，尚无人带回消息。留守的哨兵望着沟口，换防队已在壕内等候。泥水里响了一下，枪手把手放到扳机旁。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai Front · February nineteen eighteen\n\nThe post gives no answer. The duty NCO listens again. Footprints mark the low ground before the wire; scattered shots come from the German line. A light patrol enters the wet ditch, and the man behind covers the lamp.\n\nWire is broken between the outpost and headquarters. No runner has returned. Sentries watch the mouth of the ditch while the relief waits in the trench. Something stirs in the water. A gunner rests his hand beside the trigger.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on twenty-one March."), TEXT("一九一八年二月，康布雷前线在此前秋季战斗后继续修壕、换防和巡逻。雨雪在铁丝前的低地留下脚印，前哨观察德军阵位是否有变化，零星枪声打断冬季地段的安静。\n\n本连夜间派轻装巡逻队接近前哨。湿沟和相邻交通壕限制视野与行动，一处哨位没有回答，可能与通信损坏有关，也可能有敌军活动。英军哨兵继续留在阵线上，巡逻队查看前方地面，留下的人员等待他们带回情况。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 一九一八年二月\n\n哨位没有回答，值更军士又听了一会儿。铁丝前的低地留着脚印，零星枪声从德军阵地方向传来。轻装巡逻队走进湿沟，后面的人掩住灯光。\n\n前哨与连部之间有几段断线，尚无人带回消息。留守的哨兵望着沟口，换防队已在壕内等候。泥水里响了一下，枪手把手放到扳机旁。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai Front · February nineteen eighteen\n\nThe post gives no answer. The duty NCO listens again. Footprints mark the low ground before the wire; scattered shots come from the German line. A light patrol enters the wet ditch, and the man behind covers the lamp.\n\nWire is broken between the outpost and headquarters. No runner has returned. Sentries watch the mouth of the ditch while the relief waits in the trench. Something stirs in the water. A gunner rests his hand beside the trigger.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on twenty-one March."), TEXT("In February 1918, the Cambrai front remains occupied by trench repairs, reliefs and patrols after the previous autumn's battles. Rain and snow leave tracks in the low ground before the wire. Outposts watch for changes in the German positions, with intermittent firing breaking the quiet of the winter sector.\n\nThe company sends a light patrol towards the forward approaches at night. Wet ditches and nearby communication trenches limit visibility and movement. A missing reply from an outpost may reflect damaged communications or enemy activity. Sentries remain along the British line while the patrol checks the ground ahead.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 一九一八年二月"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai Front · February nineteen eighteen"), TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 一九一八年二月")},
