    {TEXT("前哨与连部之间有几段断线，尚无人带回消息。留守的哨兵望着沟口，换防队已在壕内等候。泥水里响了一下，枪手把手放到扳机旁。"), TEXT("Wire is broken between the outpost and headquarters. No runner has returned. Sentries watch the mouth of the ditch while the relief waits in the trench. Something stirs in the water. A gunner rests his hand beside the trigger."), TEXT("Wire is broken between the outpost and headquarters. No runner has returned. Sentries watch the mouth of the ditch while the relief waits in the trench. Something stirs in the water. A gunner rests his hand beside the trigger.")},
    {TEXT("三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("Germany launched Operation Michael on twenty-one March."), TEXT("三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。")},
    {TEXT("三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("Germany launched Operation Michael on twenty-one March."), TEXT("Germany launched Operation Michael on twenty-one March.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 一九一八年三月二十一日\n\n路口挤满第五集团军撤下来的人员，有人扶着伤员，有人找自己的军士。炮火打断了电话线，浓雾中的前哨已无回音。德军从支点之间穿过，枪声移向后方。\n\n后卫枪组守在道路旁，等最后一批失散人员经过。携弹手把箱子留在枪位，转身接过一副担架。军士查完眼前的人数，又向雾里望去。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · St Quentin Sector · Twenty-one March nineteen eighteen\n\nFifth Army men coming back crowd the junction. Some support wounded comrades; others ask for their NCO. Shellfire has cut the telephone wire. The posts in the fog give no answer, and German parties are passing between the strongpoints.\n\nThe rearguard gun waits beside the road for the last scattered men. A bearer leaves his ammunition at the position and takes a stretcher handle. The NCO counts those beside him, then looks into the fog again. Firing comes from farther behind.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on twenty-one March."), TEXT("一九一八年三月二十一日，米夏埃尔攻势在浓雾和猛烈炮击中压向英军前线。第五集团军守着宽阔地段，德军突击队从幸存支点之间穿过。电话交换所和道路交叉口遭到炮击，前沿报告难以送达。\n\n本连担任受威胁道路上的后卫，接应从这一地段返回的孤立部队，其中有伤员，也有与本队失散的士兵。德军沿缺口深入，威胁着受损阵位后方的联络，英军正沿剩余通路重新集结。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 一九一八年三月二十一日\n\n路口挤满第五集团军撤下来的人员，有人扶着伤员，有人找自己的军士。炮火打断了电话线，浓雾中的前哨已无回音。德军从支点之间穿过，枪声移向后方。\n\n后卫枪组守在道路旁，等最后一批失散人员经过。携弹手把箱子留在枪位，转身接过一副担架。军士查完眼前的人数，又向雾里望去。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · St Quentin Sector · Twenty-one March nineteen eighteen\n\nFifth Army men coming back crowd the junction. Some support wounded comrades; others ask for their NCO. Shellfire has cut the telephone wire. The posts in the fog give no answer, and German parties are passing between the strongpoints.\n\nThe rearguard gun waits beside the road for the last scattered men. A bearer leaves his ammunition at the position and takes a stretcher handle. The NCO counts those beside him, then looks into the fog again. Firing comes from farther behind.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on twenty-one March."), TEXT("On 21 March 1918, Operation Michael opens against the British front in dense fog and heavy bombardment. The Fifth Army holds a wide sector, where German assault parties are passing between surviving strongpoints. Telephone exchanges and road junctions are under fire, disrupting reports from the forward line.\n\nThe company serves as a rear guard along a road threatened by the advance. Isolated British parties are returning through the sector, including wounded men and troops separated from their units. German movement through the gaps threatens the communications needed to regroup behind the damaged positions.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 一九一八年三月二十一日"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · St Quentin Sector · Twenty-one March nineteen eighteen"), TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 一九一八年三月二十一日")},
