    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 斯卡尔普 · 一九一八年八月二十六日\n\n工兵在旧铁丝旁蹲下，刚翻出的炮弹还半埋在土里。加拿大部队从前方阵位经过，村边德军后卫继续射击。白垩田地上，新弹坑叠着旧弹坑。\n\n携弹队等在障碍缺口，前队沿工兵标出的通路向前。步枪手在田界卧倒，担架从他们身后送回。军士拦住一名抄近路的士兵，指向那枚露出的弹体。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Scarpe · Twenty-six August nineteen eighteen\n\nA sapper crouches beside the old wire. A shell newly exposed by the bombardment lies half buried. Canadian troops pass the forward positions while German rearguards fire from the village edge. Fresh craters overlap the older ones in the chalk.\n\nBearers wait at the gap. The leading men follow the passage the engineers have marked. Riflemen lie along a field boundary as a stretcher passes behind them. The NCO stops a man taking a shortcut and points to the exposed shell.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("一九一八年八月二十六日，斯卡尔普方向的协约国推进重返旧战线经过的白垩田野。加拿大部队越过原有阵位，德军后卫依托村落与剩余铁丝防守。炮击在接近路上翻出遗弃弹药和未爆弹。\n\n本连跟随检查受损通道的工兵。步兵在炮火支援下推进，携弹队从旧障碍缺口接近。德军枪位照看部分田界，仍在抵抗的守军与此前战斗的残骸交错分布，前进和后送伤员都受这些地段影响。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 斯卡尔普 · 一九一八年八月二十六日\n\n工兵在旧铁丝旁蹲下，刚翻出的炮弹还半埋在土里。加拿大部队从前方阵位经过，村边德军后卫继续射击。白垩田地上，新弹坑叠着旧弹坑。\n\n携弹队等在障碍缺口，前队沿工兵标出的通路向前。步枪手在田界卧倒，担架从他们身后送回。军士拦住一名抄近路的士兵，指向那枚露出的弹体。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Scarpe · Twenty-six August nineteen eighteen\n\nA sapper crouches beside the old wire. A shell newly exposed by the bombardment lies half buried. Canadian troops pass the forward positions while German rearguards fire from the village edge. Fresh craters overlap the older ones in the chalk.\n\nBearers wait at the gap. The leading men follow the passage the engineers have marked. Riflemen lie along a field boundary as a stretcher passes behind them. The NCO stops a man taking a shortcut and points to the exposed shell.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("On 26 August 1918, the Allied advance along the Scarpe returns to chalk fields crossed by earlier fronts. Canadian troops move through old positions while German rear guards defend villages and remaining wire. Shellfire has exposed abandoned ammunition and unexploded shells along routes needed by the attackers.\n\nThe company follows engineers examining the damaged passages. Infantry advance with artillery support, and ammunition parties approach through gaps in the old obstacles. German guns cover parts of the field boundaries. The sector combines active resistance with debris left by earlier fighting, affecting both movement forward and evacuation to the rear.")},
