    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 里克瓦尔 · 一九一八年九月二十九日\n\n运河两岸升起烟，陡坡上的土被炮火削落。桥还连着对岸，第四十六师的步兵从纤道上观察高处的枪位。工兵带着器材沿破坡下去，后面的人拉住绳索。\n\n下坡路只能容少数人通过，携弹队把箱子逐个传下。水面响起射击声，前队伏在岸边等候。军士挤到转弯处，抬头看了一眼那座尚完整的桥。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Riqueval · Twenty-nine September nineteen eighteen\n\nSmoke rises along the canal. Shellfire cuts earth from the steep bank. A bridge still reaches the far side. Forty-sixth Division infantry watch the guns above from the towpath. Sappers descend the broken slope with their equipment while men behind hold a rope.\n\nFew can pass down the narrow approach at once. Bearers hand their boxes from man to man. Firing crosses the water. The leading men wait against the bank, and the NCO looks up towards the bridge still standing above them.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on twenty-nine September."), TEXT("一九一八年九月二十九日，英军第四十六师进攻里克瓦尔附近的圣康坦运河明渠。澳大利亚和美军在更北的贝利库尔隧道地段进攻。陡岸、受损工事与德军掩体挡住接近线，一座完整桥梁仍连接两岸。\n\n本连在明渠和纤道旁行动。工兵借烟沿破坡工作，步兵面对俯瞰水面的阵位。有限下坡路输送人员、弹药与器材，岸上德军哨位同时威胁渡越接近地段，以及与后续英军的联系。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 里克瓦尔 · 一九一八年九月二十九日\n\n运河两岸升起烟，陡坡上的土被炮火削落。桥还连着对岸，第四十六师的步兵从纤道上观察高处的枪位。工兵带着器材沿破坡下去，后面的人拉住绳索。\n\n下坡路只能容少数人通过，携弹队把箱子逐个传下。水面响起射击声，前队伏在岸边等候。军士挤到转弯处，抬头看了一眼那座尚完整的桥。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Riqueval · Twenty-nine September nineteen eighteen\n\nSmoke rises along the canal. Shellfire cuts earth from the steep bank. A bridge still reaches the far side. Forty-sixth Division infantry watch the guns above from the towpath. Sappers descend the broken slope with their equipment while men behind hold a rope.\n\nFew can pass down the narrow approach at once. Bearers hand their boxes from man to man. Firing crosses the water. The leading men wait against the bank, and the NCO looks up towards the bridge still standing above them.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on twenty-nine September."), TEXT("On 29 September 1918, British troops of the 46th Division attack the open St Quentin Canal near Riqueval. Australian and American forces attack around the Bellicourt tunnel farther north. Steep banks, damaged earthworks and German shelters obstruct the canal approaches; an intact bridge connects the two sides.\n\nThe company operates beside the cutting and towpath. Engineers work along broken slopes under smoke, while infantry face positions overlooking the water. The restricted descents carry men, ammunition and equipment towards the crossing. German posts on the banks threaten both the approach and contact with following British troops.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 里克瓦尔 · 一九一八年九月二十九日\n\n运河两岸升起烟，陡坡上的土被炮火削落。桥还连着对岸，第四十六师的步兵从纤道上观察高处的枪位。工兵带着器材沿破坡下去，后面的人拉住绳索。\n\n下坡路只能容少数人通过，携弹队把箱子逐个传下。水面响起射击声，前队伏在岸边等候。军士挤到转弯处，抬头看了一眼那座尚完整的桥。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Riqueval · Twenty-nine September nineteen eighteen\n\nSmoke rises along the canal. Shellfire cuts earth from the steep bank. A bridge still reaches the far side. Forty-sixth Division infantry watch the guns above from the towpath. Sappers descend the broken slope with their equipment while men behind hold a rope.\n\nFew can pass down the narrow approach at once. Bearers hand their boxes from man to man. Firing crosses the water. The leading men wait against the bank, and the NCO looks up towards the bridge still standing above them.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on twenty-nine September."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 里克瓦尔 · 一九一八年九月二十九日\n\n运河两岸升起烟，陡坡上的土被炮火削落。桥还连着对岸，第四十六师的步兵从纤道上观察高处的枪位。工兵带着器材沿破坡下去，后面的人拉住绳索。\n\n下坡路只能容少数人通过，携弹队把箱子逐个传下。水面响起射击声，前队伏在岸边等候。军士挤到转弯处，抬头看了一眼那座尚完整的桥。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 里克瓦尔 · 一九一八年九月二十九日\n\n运河两岸升起烟，陡坡上的土被炮火削落。桥还连着对岸，第四十六师的步兵从纤道上观察高处的枪位。工兵带着器材沿破坡下去，后面的人拉住绳索。\n\n下坡路只能容少数人通过，携弹队把箱子逐个传下。水面响起射击声，前队伏在岸边等候。军士挤到转弯处，抬头看了一眼那座尚完整的桥。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Riqueval · Twenty-nine September nineteen eighteen\n\nSmoke rises along the canal. Shellfire cuts earth from the steep bank. A bridge still reaches the far side. Forty-sixth Division infantry watch the guns above from the towpath. Sappers descend the broken slope with their equipment while men behind hold a rope.\n\nFew can pass down the narrow approach at once. Bearers hand their boxes from man to man. Firing crosses the water. The leading men wait against the bank, and the NCO looks up towards the bridge still standing above them.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on twenty-nine September."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Riqueval · Twenty-nine September nineteen eighteen\n\nSmoke rises along the canal. Shellfire cuts earth from the steep bank. A bridge still reaches the far side, where Forty-sixth Division infantry watch the guns above the water. Sappers descend the broken slope with their equipment while men behind hold a rope.\n\nFew can pass down the narrow approach at once. Bearers hand their boxes from man to man. Firing crosses the water. The leading men wait against the bank, and the NCO looks up towards the bridge still standing above them.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on twenty-nine September.")},
