    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 一九一八年十一月初\n\n手推车停在路边，车上的包袱用绳子扎着。加拿大部队正在接近城市，居民还没有离开全部街区。观察员伏在果园边，仔细辨认残墙之间的枪口。\n\n担架队从军车旁走过，步枪手沿浅沟靠近出口。炮兵等着前沿报回位置，军士让后队暂留墙下。街道深处开了一扇门，观察员把望远镜转了过去。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Outside Valenciennes · Early November nineteen eighteen\n\nA handcart stands beside the road, its bundles tied with string. Canadian troops are approaching the town, where civilians remain in the streets. An observer lies at the orchard edge, studying a muzzle between the broken walls.\n\nA stretcher party passes the military vehicles. Riflemen follow a shallow ditch towards the exit. The batteries wait for a position from the forward posts. The NCO keeps the following men under the wall. A door opens farther down the street, and the observer turns his glasses.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("一九一八年十一月初，加拿大部队逼近瓦朗谢讷。德军外围阵位控制入城道路，城内仍住着平民。断墙、果园和浅沟限制视野，协约国炮兵观察员核对居民区附近的射界。\n\n本连在城外接近地段行动，更广地段有加拿大部队推进。军车、平民手推车和担架共用道路，德军枪位仍在出口与田界附近。战斗靠近有人居住的街道，炮火支援和后续部队通行都需要清楚辨认前方，不能仅凭远处动静判断。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 一九一八年十一月初\n\n手推车停在路边，车上的包袱用绳子扎着。加拿大部队正在接近城市，居民还没有离开全部街区。观察员伏在果园边，仔细辨认残墙之间的枪口。\n\n担架队从军车旁走过，步枪手沿浅沟靠近出口。炮兵等着前沿报回位置，军士让后队暂留墙下。街道深处开了一扇门，观察员把望远镜转了过去。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Outside Valenciennes · Early November nineteen eighteen\n\nA handcart stands beside the road, its bundles tied with string. Canadian troops are approaching the town, where civilians remain in the streets. An observer lies at the orchard edge, studying a muzzle between the broken walls.\n\nA stretcher party passes the military vehicles. Riflemen follow a shallow ditch towards the exit. The batteries wait for a position from the forward posts. The NCO keeps the following men under the wall. A door opens farther down the street, and the observer turns his glasses.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("Canadian troops approach Valenciennes at the beginning of November 1918. German positions around the outskirts cover the roads into a town still inhabited by civilians. Broken walls, orchards and shallow ditches limit observation, while Allied artillery observers check the firing areas near the settlement.\n\nThe company operates on these outer approaches beside Canadian formations in the wider sector. Military vehicles, civilian carts and stretchers share the roads. German guns remain near the exits and field boundaries. The fighting takes place close to occupied streets, where artillery support and the movement of following troops depend on careful observation.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 一九一八年十一月初"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Outside Valenciennes · Early November nineteen eighteen"), TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 一九一八年十一月初")},
