    {TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 一九一七年四月九日\n\n前哨的电话只有杂音。雨雪遮住白垩坡，英军已越过被炮击打断的前沿。洞穴里的士兵重新携枪出壕，枪位向连部报来缺弹。\n\n反击队在白垩路旁集合。联络兵循断线找去，坡后的机枪继续射击。携弹手把箱子搬过担架，几个失联哨位尚未报回点名结果。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Arras · Nine April nineteen seventeen\n\nThe outpost telephone gives only static. Sleet hides the chalk slope and British troops have crossed the damaged forward line. Men come out of the caves with their rifles. The gun posts report that ammunition is running short.\n\nCounterattack parties assemble beside the chalk road. A runner follows the broken wire while the guns beyond the crest keep firing. Bearers carry their boxes past stretchers. Several silent posts have yet to return their rolls.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("一九一七年四月九日，英军在阿拉斯的进攻打乱了德军前沿。雨雪和炮火遮住白垩坡面，洞穴与壕沟仍联系着部分阵位，前哨电话却只剩杂音，数处枪位已与后方失联。\n\n本连沿白垩路集结，准备实施局部反击。这一地段包括山脊接近线，以及向幸存哨位输送弹药的通路。英军越过受损的前沿壕沟，坡后的德军枪组继续射击。前线各支点情况不一，人员和补给仍须通过高地两侧。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 一九一七年四月九日\n\n前哨的电话只有杂音。雨雪遮住白垩坡，英军已越过被炮击打断的前沿。洞穴里的士兵重新携枪出壕，枪位向连部报来缺弹。\n\n反击队在白垩路旁集合。联络兵循断线找去，坡后的机枪继续射击。携弹手把箱子搬过担架，几个失联哨位尚未报回点名结果。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Arras · Nine April nineteen seventeen\n\nThe outpost telephone gives only static. Sleet hides the chalk slope and British troops have crossed the damaged forward line. Men come out of the caves with their rifles. The gun posts report that ammunition is running short.\n\nCounterattack parties assemble beside the chalk road. A runner follows the broken wire while the guns beyond the crest keep firing. Bearers carry their boxes past stretchers. Several silent posts have yet to return their rolls.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("The British attack at Arras on 9 April 1917 has disrupted the German forward line. Rain, snow and bombardment obscure the chalk slopes. Some posts remain connected through caves and trenches, but the outpost telephone gives only interference, and several gun positions have lost contact with the rear.\n\nThe company is assembling a local counterattack along the chalk road. Its sector includes the ridge approaches and the routes supplying the surviving posts. British troops are advancing beyond the damaged front trenches, while German crews behind the high ground try to maintain fire and restore contact.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 一九一七年四月九日"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Arras · Nine April nineteen seventeen"), TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 一九一七年四月九日")},
