    {TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 一九一七年四月中旬\n\n地下掩体的出口落满碎砖，换防人员弯腰钻出。化工厂外已有英军接近，枪手隔着断墙观察壕口。电话线穿过厂房废墟，接线兵只找到一截断头。\n\n反击队沿铁路堤下集合，携弹兵把箱子交给仍在射击的枪组。军士指着被炮火切断的交通壕，重新安排去路。厂墙另一面的脚步听得很近。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April nineteen seventeen\n\nBricks cover the dugout exit. Reliefs bend low to come out. British troops are approaching the chemical works, and a gunner watches the trench mouth through a broken wall. The linesman finds only a severed end among the factory ruins.\n\nCounterattack parties assemble below the railway bank. Bearers hand boxes to a gun still firing. The NCO points to the communication trench cut by shellfire and directs men along another passage. Footsteps sound close on the other side of the wall.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until sixteen May."), TEXT("一九一七年四月中旬，勒厄化工厂仍是阿拉斯以东道路上的德军支点。英军正在进入外围接近地段。厂墙、铁路工事和地下掩体构成相连阵位，炮火却已损坏其间通道。\n\n本连准备向受威胁的外围壕沟反击。枪组隔着破墙照看缺口，携弹兵使用尚存掩蔽路线。接近壕关系着厂区交通，一旦中断，部分阵位就难以接到换防人员和弹药。铁路堤与残墙分割视野，守军无法从一处看清整片外围。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 一九一七年四月中旬\n\n地下掩体的出口落满碎砖，换防人员弯腰钻出。化工厂外已有英军接近，枪手隔着断墙观察壕口。电话线穿过厂房废墟，接线兵只找到一截断头。\n\n反击队沿铁路堤下集合，携弹兵把箱子交给仍在射击的枪组。军士指着被炮火切断的交通壕，重新安排去路。厂墙另一面的脚步听得很近。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April nineteen seventeen\n\nBricks cover the dugout exit. Reliefs bend low to come out. British troops are approaching the chemical works, and a gunner watches the trench mouth through a broken wall. The linesman finds only a severed end among the factory ruins.\n\nCounterattack parties assemble below the railway bank. Bearers hand boxes to a gun still firing. The NCO points to the communication trench cut by shellfire and directs men along another passage. Footsteps sound close on the other side of the wall.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until sixteen May."), TEXT("The chemical works at Roeux remain a German strongpoint on the roads east of Arras. In mid-April 1917, British troops are pressing into the outer approaches. Factory walls, railway earthworks and underground shelters give the defenders connected positions, although shellfire has damaged the passages between them.\n\nThe company's counterattack is directed towards the threatened outer trenches. Gun crews cover gaps through the broken masonry, and ammunition bearers use the remaining sheltered routes. Loss of an approach trench would interrupt traffic to the works, leaving some factory positions separated from their reliefs and supplies.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 一九一七年四月中旬"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April nineteen seventeen"), TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 一九一七年四月中旬")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 一九一七年四月中旬"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April nineteen seventeen"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April nineteen seventeen")},
