    {TEXT("阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("The Arras offensive continued until sixteen May."), TEXT("The Arras offensive continued until sixteen May.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 一九一七年五月三日\n\n掩蔽部里响起上壕的口令，枪榴弹正在胸墙外爆炸。铁丝之间还压着四月留下的残骸，英澳步兵又从缺口接近。枪组把弹带拖到射位旁边。\n\n携弹兵贴着深壕前送，换防队在转角停步。相邻哨位只见烟尘，军士让一名联络兵过去查看。坡面上露出钢盔又消失，枪手转动枪架追着看。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bullecourt · Three May nineteen seventeen\n\nThe order to man the trench reaches the dugout as rifle grenades burst outside the parapet. April's wreckage still weighs down the wire. British and Australian infantry approach its gaps again. The crew pulls a belt beside the mounting.\n\nBearers follow the deep trench while reliefs halt at a traverse. Smoke hides the neighbouring post. The NCO sends a runner to find it. A helmet appears above the slope and disappears; the gunner turns his mounting to search the ground again.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("一九一七年五月三日，澳大利亚与英国部队在布勒库尔重新进攻。德军仍守着兴登堡线铁丝后的纵深壕，四月战斗留下的残骸尚未清走。后方通道把弹药和换防人员送往幸存哨位。\n\n本连位于这套壕沟的一段，分散枪组照看铁丝受损地段，枪榴弹正落向壕角和胸墙。英澳步兵沿缺口接近。地下掩体支撑着防御，但外围壕沟遭到攻击，相邻哨位的联系也受威胁。断墙与弹坑使接近者时隐时现。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 一九一七年五月三日\n\n掩蔽部里响起上壕的口令，枪榴弹正在胸墙外爆炸。铁丝之间还压着四月留下的残骸，英澳步兵又从缺口接近。枪组把弹带拖到射位旁边。\n\n携弹兵贴着深壕前送，换防队在转角停步。相邻哨位只见烟尘，军士让一名联络兵过去查看。坡面上露出钢盔又消失，枪手转动枪架追着看。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bullecourt · Three May nineteen seventeen\n\nThe order to man the trench reaches the dugout as rifle grenades burst outside the parapet. April's wreckage still weighs down the wire. British and Australian infantry approach its gaps again. The crew pulls a belt beside the mounting.\n\nBearers follow the deep trench while reliefs halt at a traverse. Smoke hides the neighbouring post. The NCO sends a runner to find it. A helmet appears above the slope and disappears; the gunner turns his mounting to search the ground again.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("Australian and British attacks resume at Bullecourt on 3 May 1917. German defenders still hold deep trenches behind the Hindenburg wire, where the wreckage of the April battle remains. Rear passages carry ammunition and reliefs towards posts that survived the earlier fighting.\n\nThe company occupies part of this trench system. Its dispersed guns cover damaged sections of wire, while rifle grenades are falling around the corners and parapets. British and Australian infantry are approaching the gaps. The shelter network supports the defence, but bombardment and attacks on the outer trenches threaten contact between adjacent posts.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 一九一七年五月三日"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bullecourt · Three May nineteen seventeen"), TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 一九一七年五月三日")},
