    {TEXT("第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("The Third Battle of Ypres began on thirty-one July."), TEXT("The Third Battle of Ypres began on thirty-one July.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 一九一七年八月\n\n混凝土顶上落下灰尘，枪手把眼睛贴回射孔。农场外的田野已经积水，英军沿干路接近。送弹路经过掩体旁，换防人员侧身从弹箱之间穿过。\n\n迫击炮弹落在残墙后面，联络兵听不清邻哨的回答。军士让枪组继续守着入口，自己沿墙走到拐角。水面晃着几个倒影，干路上的脚步却停了。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Langemarck · August nineteen seventeen\n\nDust falls from the concrete roof. The gunner returns his eye to the loophole. Water covers the field outside the farm, and British troops follow the dry approaches. Reliefs squeeze past ammunition boxes on the track beside the shelter.\n\nMortar bombs fall behind the ruined wall. A runner cannot hear the next post's reply. The NCO leaves the crew watching the entrance and follows the wall to its corner. Reflections move on the water, but footsteps on the dry track have stopped.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("一九一七年八月，朗厄马尔克的德军依靠混凝土掩体守住积水田野。农场建筑已成废墟，部分有遮蔽的枪位仍由干路联系。伊普尔周边战斗继续，英军正从据点之间接近。\n\n本连位于这条分散防线的一段，中央送弹路供给邻近枪组和换防队，机枪照看农场周围入口。积水隔开原先较易联系的阵位，英军迫击炮和接近干路的进攻威胁补给运输。前沿各处仍能抵抗，却不能在一处看清全部接近地段。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 一九一七年八月\n\n混凝土顶上落下灰尘，枪手把眼睛贴回射孔。农场外的田野已经积水，英军沿干路接近。送弹路经过掩体旁，换防人员侧身从弹箱之间穿过。\n\n迫击炮弹落在残墙后面，联络兵听不清邻哨的回答。军士让枪组继续守着入口，自己沿墙走到拐角。水面晃着几个倒影，干路上的脚步却停了。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Langemarck · August nineteen seventeen\n\nDust falls from the concrete roof. The gunner returns his eye to the loophole. Water covers the field outside the farm, and British troops follow the dry approaches. Reliefs squeeze past ammunition boxes on the track beside the shelter.\n\nMortar bombs fall behind the ruined wall. A runner cannot hear the next post's reply. The NCO leaves the crew watching the entrance and follows the wall to its corner. Reflections move on the water, but footsteps on the dry track have stopped.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("At Langemarck in August 1917, concrete shelters support the German defence across waterlogged fields. Farm buildings have been reduced to ruins, but some protected gun positions remain connected by dry tracks. British troops are approaching between the strongpoints as the fighting around Ypres continues.\n\nThe company occupies part of this dispersed line. The central ammunition route serves neighbouring crews and relief parties, while guns cover the approaches around ruined farms. Flooding has separated positions that once had easier contact. British mortar fire and attacks near the tracks threaten the movement needed to keep those posts supplied.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 一九一七年八月"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Langemarck · August nineteen seventeen"), TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 一九一七年八月")},
