    {TEXT("伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("The Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("The Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 一九一七年九月\n\n观察员摊开图纸，把前沿标记向林后移了一点。英军炮火还在延伸，新胸墙已出现在树桩之间。预备队沿破路进入林地，枪组停下来等候侧翼消息。\n\n幸存哨位夹在两军之间，携弹兵不知道该在哪个壕口转弯。军士向断树后打出手势，前队逐人穿过开阔处。观察员的铅笔仍压在那条刚画出的线上。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Menin Road · September nineteen seventeen\n\nThe observer opens his sketch and shifts a forward mark farther into the wood. British shellfire continues to lift. New parapets appear among the stumps. Reserves enter along a broken path; the gun crew stops for news from the flank.\n\nSurviving posts lie between the forces. A bearer is unsure which trench mouth to take. The NCO signals beyond a shattered tree, and the leading men cross the open patch one at a time. The observer's pencil rests on his fresh line.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("一九一七年九月，英军在梅宁路以强大炮火支援有限推进。德军预备队在破碎林地后方集结反击，报告称英军正在林缘加固新阵位。尚存小路和坡脊限制着接近方向。\n\n本连从后方进入受威胁地段。炮兵观察员核对变化中的战线，枪组照看穿林路线。幸存德军哨位仍隔在英军推进部队与预备队之间。交通壕和小路受损，增援与弹药难以及时抵达，林间残树又遮住了部分相邻阵位。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 一九一七年九月\n\n观察员摊开图纸，把前沿标记向林后移了一点。英军炮火还在延伸，新胸墙已出现在树桩之间。预备队沿破路进入林地，枪组停下来等候侧翼消息。\n\n幸存哨位夹在两军之间，携弹兵不知道该在哪个壕口转弯。军士向断树后打出手势，前队逐人穿过开阔处。观察员的铅笔仍压在那条刚画出的线上。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Menin Road · September nineteen seventeen\n\nThe observer opens his sketch and shifts a forward mark farther into the wood. British shellfire continues to lift. New parapets appear among the stumps. Reserves enter along a broken path; the gun crew stops for news from the flank.\n\nSurviving posts lie between the forces. A bearer is unsure which trench mouth to take. The NCO signals beyond a shattered tree, and the leading men cross the open patch one at a time. The observer's pencil rests on his fresh line.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("The British advance at the Menin Road in September 1917 is taking limited ground under heavy artillery cover. German reserves are assembling beyond the shattered woodland for a counterattack. Reports describe British troops strengthening new positions near the tree line, where surviving paths and ridges restrict the approaches.\n\nThe company moves from the rear towards this threatened sector. Artillery observers are checking the changing line, and gun crews cover routes through the woods. Surviving German posts remain between the British advance and the reserves. Broken communications and damaged tracks complicate the arrival of reinforcements and ammunition.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 一九一七年九月"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Menin Road · September nineteen seventeen"), TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 一九一七年九月")},
