    {TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 一九一八年四月二十四日\n\n村口的战车转向路口，步兵借着车侧经过果园。英军装甲在近郊开火，断墙后也有步枪声。车组看不见小巷，前队停在墙角，等后面的人靠近。\n\n携弹兵沿村道赶来，军士让一班步枪手进入侧巷。履带声绕过建筑又传回来，车影已经被挡住。门洞里一阵射击，走在最前面的人立刻贴住砖墙。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · Twenty-four April nineteen eighteen\n\nA tank turns at the village entrance and infantry pass the orchard beside its flank. British armour fires from the outskirts. Rifles answer behind a broken wall. The crew cannot see the lane, where the leading men wait for those behind.\n\nBearers arrive along the village road. The NCO sends a section into a side alley. Tracks can be heard beyond the buildings, but the vehicle is hidden. A burst comes from a doorway and the first rifleman presses against the bricks.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("一九一八年四月二十四日，德军进攻来到维莱布勒托讷，这里控制着通往亚眠铁路中心的道路。步兵和坦克进入村庄，英军装甲从近郊开火。破损建筑与果园边界把战斗分成短促、半隐蔽的接近地段。\n\n本连在德军车辆周围行动，随着它们向村口移动。墙巷之间仍有英军步兵，部分位置不在车组视野内。村道输送后续人员和弹药，建筑与交叉路遮住移动，装甲与步兵时常失去直接观察。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 一九一八年四月二十四日\n\n村口的战车转向路口，步兵借着车侧经过果园。英军装甲在近郊开火，断墙后也有步枪声。车组看不见小巷，前队停在墙角，等后面的人靠近。\n\n携弹兵沿村道赶来，军士让一班步枪手进入侧巷。履带声绕过建筑又传回来，车影已经被挡住。门洞里一阵射击，走在最前面的人立刻贴住砖墙。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · Twenty-four April nineteen eighteen\n\nA tank turns at the village entrance and infantry pass the orchard beside its flank. British armour fires from the outskirts. Rifles answer behind a broken wall. The crew cannot see the lane, where the leading men wait for those behind.\n\nBearers arrive along the village road. The NCO sends a section into a side alley. Tracks can be heard beyond the buildings, but the vehicle is hidden. A burst comes from a doorway and the first rifleman presses against the bricks.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("The German attack on 24 April 1918 reaches Villers-Bretonneux, which guards roads towards the Amiens railway centre. Infantry and tanks enter the village while British armour fires from the nearby outskirts. Broken buildings and orchard boundaries divide the fighting into short, partly concealed approaches.\n\nThe company operates around the German vehicles as they move towards the village exits. British infantry remain among the walls and lanes, beyond parts of the tank crews' view. Roads through the settlement carry following troops and ammunition. Contact between armour and infantry is interrupted when movement passes behind buildings or across junctions.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 一九一八年四月二十四日"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · Twenty-four April nineteen eighteen"), TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 一九一八年四月二十四日")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 一九一八年四月二十四日"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · Twenty-four April nineteen eighteen"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · Twenty-four April nineteen eighteen")},
    {TEXT("村口的战车转向路口，步兵借着车侧经过果园。英军装甲在近郊开火，断墙后也有步枪声。车组看不见小巷，前队停在墙角，等后面的人靠近。"), TEXT("A tank turns at the village entrance and infantry pass the orchard beside its flank. British armour fires from the outskirts. Rifles answer behind a broken wall. The crew cannot see the lane, where the leading men wait for those behind."), TEXT("村口的战车转向路口，步兵借着车侧经过果园。英军装甲在近郊开火，断墙后也有步枪声。车组看不见小巷，前队停在墙角，等后面的人靠近。")},
    {TEXT("村口的战车转向路口，步兵借着车侧经过果园。英军装甲在近郊开火，断墙后也有步枪声。车组看不见小巷，前队停在墙角，等后面的人靠近。"), TEXT("A tank turns at the village entrance and infantry pass the orchard beside its flank. British armour fires from the outskirts. Rifles answer behind a broken wall. The crew cannot see the lane, where the leading men wait for those behind."), TEXT("A tank turns at the village entrance and infantry pass the orchard beside its flank. British armour fires from the outskirts. Rifles answer behind a broken wall. The crew cannot see the lane, where the leading men wait for those behind.")},
    {TEXT("携弹兵沿村道赶来，军士让一班步枪手进入侧巷。履带声绕过建筑又传回来，车影已经被挡住。门洞里一阵射击，走在最前面的人立刻贴住砖墙。"), TEXT("Bearers arrive along the village road. The NCO sends a section into a side alley. Tracks can be heard beyond the buildings, but the vehicle is hidden. A burst comes from a doorway and the first rifleman presses against the bricks."), TEXT("携弹兵沿村道赶来，军士让一班步枪手进入侧巷。履带声绕过建筑又传回来，车影已经被挡住。门洞里一阵射击，走在最前面的人立刻贴住砖墙。")},
    {TEXT("携弹兵沿村道赶来，军士让一班步枪手进入侧巷。履带声绕过建筑又传回来，车影已经被挡住。门洞里一阵射击，走在最前面的人立刻贴住砖墙。"), TEXT("Bearers arrive along the village road. The NCO sends a section into a side alley. Tracks can be heard beyond the buildings, but the vehicle is hidden. A burst comes from a doorway and the first rifleman presses against the bricks."), TEXT("Bearers arrive along the village road. The NCO sends a section into a side alley. Tracks can be heard beyond the buildings, but the vehicle is hidden. A burst comes from a doorway and the first rifleman presses against the bricks.")},
    {TEXT("这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("The first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。")},
    {TEXT("这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("The first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("The first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 一九一八年八月八日\n\n前哨的报告上写着战车，送信的人却说不清邻队在哪里。雾中的田野传来发动机声，路口挤满返回部队。反坦克枪组把器材放下，朝来路寻找射位。\n\n机枪掩护孤立阵位撤出的人，增援在另一侧逆向通过。军士把携弹手叫到残墙下，逐个问前面的情况。一名满身泥土的士兵指向雾里，手仍没有放下。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Amiens · Eight August nineteen eighteen\n\nThe report names tanks, but its runner cannot place the neighbouring unit. Engines sound across the misty fields. Returning troops crowd the junction. The anti-tank crew lowers its equipment and searches for a position facing the approach.\n\nA machine gun covers men leaving isolated posts while reinforcements pass the other way. The NCO calls bearers under the ruined wall and asks each about the front. One soldier covered in mud points into the mist. His arm stays raised as more men pass.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("一九一八年八月八日，亚眠以东的协约国进攻切断德军前哨之间的通信。雾遮住田野动静，步兵与坦克的报告从前线各处送来。后方道路挤满返回部队，增援仍试图逆向前行。\n\n本连在后卫所需的通路附近交战，机枪与反坦克组聚在路口，掩护离开孤立阵位的人。有些哨位仍在视线之外抵抗，炮击破坏和协约国压力威胁着撤离与补给共用的道路。各队对邻近地段的掌握并不完整。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 一九一八年八月八日\n\n前哨的报告上写着战车，送信的人却说不清邻队在哪里。雾中的田野传来发动机声，路口挤满返回部队。反坦克枪组把器材放下，朝来路寻找射位。\n\n机枪掩护孤立阵位撤出的人，增援在另一侧逆向通过。军士把携弹手叫到残墙下，逐个问前面的情况。一名满身泥土的士兵指向雾里，手仍没有放下。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Amiens · Eight August nineteen eighteen\n\nThe report names tanks, but its runner cannot place the neighbouring unit. Engines sound across the misty fields. Returning troops crowd the junction. The anti-tank crew lowers its equipment and searches for a position facing the approach.\n\nA machine gun covers men leaving isolated posts while reinforcements pass the other way. The NCO calls bearers under the ruined wall and asks each about the front. One soldier covered in mud points into the mist. His arm stays raised as more men pass.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("The Allied attack east of Amiens on 8 August 1918 is cutting communications between German forward posts. Mist obscures movement across the fields, while reports of infantry and tanks arrive from different parts of the front. Rear roads fill with withdrawing troops as reinforcements try to move forward.\n\nThe company is engaged around routes needed by the rear guard. Machine gun and anti-tank crews gather near road junctions, covering men coming out of isolated positions. Some posts remain active beyond the company's view. Artillery damage and Allied pressure threaten the passages carrying both the withdrawal and German supplies.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 一九一八年八月八日"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Amiens · Eight August nineteen eighteen"), TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 一九一八年八月八日")},
