    {TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 一九一八年八月下旬\n\n旧铁丝横在撤回路上，工兵蹲下把断股搬开。加拿大部队已穿过前方阵位，村边的枪组还在射击。炮火又翻出遗弃弹药，白垩土里露着一枚弹尖。\n\n携弹队与换防人员在田界碰面，伤员从窄路中间送走。军士先让担架过去，再叫后面的人沿沟走。枪手回头找自己的携弹兵，路口已被车辆堵住。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Scarpe · Late August nineteen eighteen\n\nOld wire crosses the withdrawal route. A pioneer crouches to move the broken strands. Canadian troops have passed the forward works, and guns still fire beside the village. Shellfire exposes abandoned ammunition, leaving a pointed shell in the chalk.\n\nBearers meet reliefs at a field boundary while wounded men pass between them. The NCO lets a stretcher through first, then directs the others along the ditch. A gunner turns to find his bearer, but vehicles have blocked the junction behind the position.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("一九一八年八月下旬，斯卡尔普沿线德军后卫面对协约国在白垩地带的再次推进。加拿大部队越过旧阵位，接近后方村落与道路。早先铁丝和遗弃弹药如今也挡住德军撤回路线。\n\n本连在这些旧工事周围掩护后方交通，工兵查看障碍，机枪组占住接近地段。受损田界提供遮蔽，却藏着未爆弹并打断行进。弹药、换防队和伤员仍从这里经过，协约国压力正在传到相邻地段，道路逐渐拥挤。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 一九一八年八月下旬\n\n旧铁丝横在撤回路上，工兵蹲下把断股搬开。加拿大部队已穿过前方阵位，村边的枪组还在射击。炮火又翻出遗弃弹药，白垩土里露着一枚弹尖。\n\n携弹队与换防人员在田界碰面，伤员从窄路中间送走。军士先让担架过去，再叫后面的人沿沟走。枪手回头找自己的携弹兵，路口已被车辆堵住。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Scarpe · Late August nineteen eighteen\n\nOld wire crosses the withdrawal route. A pioneer crouches to move the broken strands. Canadian troops have passed the forward works, and guns still fire beside the village. Shellfire exposes abandoned ammunition, leaving a pointed shell in the chalk.\n\nBearers meet reliefs at a field boundary while wounded men pass between them. The NCO lets a stretcher through first, then directs the others along the ditch. A gunner turns to find his bearer, but vehicles have blocked the junction behind the position.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("In late August 1918, German rear guards along the Scarpe face a renewed Allied advance through the chalk country. Canadian troops are crossing old positions towards villages and roads behind the line. Earlier wire and discarded ammunition now obstruct routes also needed by withdrawing German units.\n\nThe company covers part of the rearward traffic through these former works. Engineers examine obstacles while machine gun crews occupy positions near the approaches. Damaged field boundaries provide cover but conceal unexploded shells and interrupt movement. Ammunition, reliefs and wounded men continue to pass as Allied pressure reaches the neighbouring sectors.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 一九一八年八月下旬"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Scarpe · Late August nineteen eighteen"), TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 一九一八年八月下旬")},
