    {TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 一九一八年十一月初\n\n枪组身旁经过一辆平民手推车，车轮在碎砖上颠簸。加拿大部队正向外围逼近，后卫还守着出口。换防人员沿果园过来，其他部队从残墙后退向城外。\n\n路上挤着伤员和军车，军士不断示意前面继续走。步枪手伏在浅沟里等候，墙另一侧有射击声。手推车卡在一块砖上，旁边的人伸手扶了一把。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Outside Valenciennes · Early November nineteen eighteen\n\nA civilian handcart passes the gun, its wheels jolting over broken bricks. Canadian troops approach the outskirts while the rearguard holds the exit. Reliefs come through the orchard and other parties withdraw beyond the ruined walls.\n\nWounded men and military vehicles fill the road. The NCO keeps signalling those ahead to move. Riflemen wait in a shallow ditch, hearing shots beyond the wall. The handcart catches on a brick beside them; a passing man reaches over to steady its loaded frame.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("一九一八年十一月初，加拿大部队逼近瓦朗谢讷，德军从城镇接近地段后撤。枪位照看外围公路和出口，城内仍有平民，手推车、军车与伤员一起经过城郊。各条道路的交通仍在继续。\n\n本连担任这里的后卫，换防人员接近枪组，其他部队则从断墙和果园之间向后移动。短促接近线限制观察，加拿大部队对邻近阵位的压力威胁着撤退纵队与补给所需路线。居民区旁的残墙还遮住了部分前方动静。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 一九一八年十一月初\n\n枪组身旁经过一辆平民手推车，车轮在碎砖上颠簸。加拿大部队正向外围逼近，后卫还守着出口。换防人员沿果园过来，其他部队从残墙后退向城外。\n\n路上挤着伤员和军车，军士不断示意前面继续走。步枪手伏在浅沟里等候，墙另一侧有射击声。手推车卡在一块砖上，旁边的人伸手扶了一把。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Outside Valenciennes · Early November nineteen eighteen\n\nA civilian handcart passes the gun, its wheels jolting over broken bricks. Canadian troops approach the outskirts while the rearguard holds the exit. Reliefs come through the orchard and other parties withdraw beyond the ruined walls.\n\nWounded men and military vehicles fill the road. The NCO keeps signalling those ahead to move. Riflemen wait in a shallow ditch, hearing shots beyond the wall. The handcart catches on a brick beside them; a passing man reaches over to steady its loaded frame.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("At the beginning of November 1918, Canadian troops are advancing towards Valenciennes as German forces withdraw through the town's approaches. Gun positions cover the outer roads and exits. Civilians remain in the settlement, and carts, military vehicles and wounded men share the traffic moving through the outskirts.\n\nThe company serves in this rear guard. Relief parties approach the guns while other troops move towards the rear, passing between broken walls and orchards. Observation is limited across the short approaches. Canadian pressure on nearby positions threatens routes still needed by the withdrawing columns and their supplies.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 一九一八年十一月初"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Outside Valenciennes · Early November nineteen eighteen"), TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 一九一八年十一月初")},
