    {TEXT("加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("Canadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("Canadian troops took Valenciennes in early November.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 桑布尔接近地 · 一九一八年十一月四日\n\n后卫机枪朝着运河渡口，预备队留在路口等人。别处停战的消息到了，今天的撤离命令也到了。城郊公路上，居民推着家当夹在撤回的纵队之间。\n\n前哨还有人员没有回来，携弹兵把剩余箱子放在墙下。军士望着来路，示意最后一队先通过障碍。枪手握住已经发热的握把，河岸那边又传来步枪声。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Sambre Approaches · Four November nineteen eighteen\n\nThe rearguard gun faces the canal crossing. Reserves wait at the junction for men still forward. News of armistices elsewhere has arrived with today's withdrawal orders. Civilians push their belongings between the returning columns on the outskirts road.\n\nSome men remain at the outposts. Bearers put their last boxes under a wall. The NCO watches the approach and signals another party through the damaged obstacles. The gunner holds the warm grips. Rifle fire sounds again from the bank beyond the crossing.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at eleven on eleven November."), TEXT("一九一八年十一月四日，其他战场停战的消息到了德军后方，西线仍在交战。协约国接近桑布尔渡口与附近居民区，新西兰部队在另一段战线逼近勒凯努瓦，德军纵队继续后撤。\n\n本连在运河接近地段掩护一条局部退路。机枪组守望渡口，预备队等待从前哨返回的人员。平民和军队共用城郊公路，受损障碍与协约国压力拖慢通行。后卫仍依靠这些狭路接应未撤出的部队，并运走剩余物资。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 桑布尔接近地 · 一九一八年十一月四日\n\n后卫机枪朝着运河渡口，预备队留在路口等人。别处停战的消息到了，今天的撤离命令也到了。城郊公路上，居民推着家当夹在撤回的纵队之间。\n\n前哨还有人员没有回来，携弹兵把剩余箱子放在墙下。军士望着来路，示意最后一队先通过障碍。枪手握住已经发热的握把，河岸那边又传来步枪声。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Sambre Approaches · Four November nineteen eighteen\n\nThe rearguard gun faces the canal crossing. Reserves wait at the junction for men still forward. News of armistices elsewhere has arrived with today's withdrawal orders. Civilians push their belongings between the returning columns on the outskirts road.\n\nSome men remain at the outposts. Bearers put their last boxes under a wall. The NCO watches the approach and signals another party through the damaged obstacles. The gunner holds the warm grips. Rifle fire sounds again from the bank beyond the crossing.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at eleven on eleven November."), TEXT("By 4 November 1918, news of armistices in other theatres has reached the German rear, but the Western Front continues fighting. Allied troops are approaching the Sambre crossings and nearby settlements. Elsewhere along the front, New Zealand forces are nearing Le Quesnoy as German columns move back.\n\nThe company covers a local withdrawal route beside the canal approaches. Machine gun crews watch the crossings, and reserves wait for parties returning from forward posts. Civilian and military traffic share the roads through the outskirts. Damaged obstacles and Allied pressure slow movement along passages still needed by the German rear guard.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 桑布尔接近地 · 一九一八年十一月四日"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Sambre Approaches · Four November nineteen eighteen"), TEXT("战时日志 · 桑布尔接近地 · 一九一八年十一月四日")},
