    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 沃堡外围 · 一九一六年六月\n\n战报攥在联络兵手里，村口的空地却过不去。德军已压近堡垒外围，残墙之间仍有法军枪位射击。换防队伏在墙下，等前沿的人指出一条通路。\n\n机枪转向废墟缺口，步枪手沿墙根分开。军士让联络兵留在近处，自己探头观察对面的壕口。堡垒还在更远的地方，眼前一段村道已经落满弹屑。\n\n沃堡在六月落入德军之手。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Outside Fort Vaux · June nineteen sixteen\n\nThe runner holds his report but cannot cross the open ground at the village entrance. German troops press the fort's outer positions. French guns still fire between ruined walls. The relief waits below the masonry for a passage forward.\n\nA machine gun turns towards a gap in the ruins. Riflemen spread along the wall. The NCO keeps the runner close and looks towards the opposite trench mouth. The fort lies farther away; fragments already cover the short village road before them.\n\nFort Vaux fell to German troops in June."), TEXT("一九一六年六月，德军在凡尔登默兹河东岸继续进攻，战斗逼近沃堡。法国外围阵地受到压力，堡垒与邻近防线之间的联络也遭到威胁。村口仍有残墙可作掩体，前哨与后方联络点之间却隔着暴露的空地。\n\n本连所在的是堡外村落地段，步枪与机枪火力能够射入废墟之间的缺口。敌军压向村口时，即使尚未抵达堡垒，也可能割断外围哨位。接替人员和战报往返前后，都要经过这片受火力监视的地面。")},
    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 沃堡外围 · 一九一六年六月\n\n战报攥在联络兵手里，村口的空地却过不去。德军已压近堡垒外围，残墙之间仍有法军枪位射击。换防队伏在墙下，等前沿的人指出一条通路。\n\n机枪转向废墟缺口，步枪手沿墙根分开。军士让联络兵留在近处，自己探头观察对面的壕口。堡垒还在更远的地方，眼前一段村道已经落满弹屑。\n\n沃堡在六月落入德军之手。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Outside Fort Vaux · June nineteen sixteen\n\nThe runner holds his report but cannot cross the open ground at the village entrance. German troops press the fort's outer positions. French guns still fire between ruined walls. The relief waits below the masonry for a passage forward.\n\nA machine gun turns towards a gap in the ruins. Riflemen spread along the wall. The NCO keeps the runner close and looks towards the opposite trench mouth. The fort lies farther away; fragments already cover the short village road before them.\n\nFort Vaux fell to German troops in June."), TEXT("By June 1916, German attacks at Verdun are pressing towards Fort Vaux on the eastern bank of the Meuse. Fighting around the fort threatens the French outer defences and their communications. The village approaches contain ruined walls, but open ground separates the outposts from the liaison point behind them.\n\nThe company is assigned to this outer sector, where rifle and machine-gun fire reaches the gaps between the ruins. Pressure on the village can isolate the posts without reaching the fort itself. Reinforcements and reports must cross the exposed ground between the village and the rear.")},
    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 沃堡外围 · 一九一六年六月"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Outside Fort Vaux · June nineteen sixteen"), TEXT("行军作战日志 · 沃堡外围 · 一九一六年六月")},
