    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 杜奥蒙外围 · 一九一六年十月二十四日\n\n炮火越过堡垒下方的坡面，反攻开始。德军自二月占着杜奥蒙，铁丝横在上坡路上。先头队伏于弹坑，等工兵把剪钳送到壕口。\n\n坡脊挡住了后面的枪位。携弹手贴着坑岸前送，军士沿两条接近路传下出发口令。电话线拖过积水，接线兵跪在泥里；连部等着第一声来自高处的回话。\n\n法军在这次反攻中收复杜奥蒙堡垒。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Outside Douaumont · Twenty-four October nineteen sixteen\n\nThe guns lift over the slope below the fort and the counteroffensive opens. German troops have held Douaumont since February. Wire crosses the uphill approaches. The leading men lie in shell holes while the sappers bring their cutters to the trench mouth.\n\nThe crest hides the guns behind it. Bearers follow the crater banks. Orders pass down both approaches. A telephone wire drags through water; the linesman kneels in the mud. Headquarters waits for the first answer from the heights.\n\nFrench forces recovered Fort Douaumont in this counteroffensive."), TEXT("一九一六年十月二十四日，法军在凡尔登北面的杜奥蒙周围展开反攻。堡垒自二月起由德军占据，法军炮火准备先于步兵向周围高地推进。数月轰击已经破坏坡地，德军防御仍依托这片起伏地面展开。\n\n本连位于堡垒下方的外围斜坡。两条上坡道路受到铁丝网阻挡，山脊遮住一部分敌军阵线，较近阵地后面仍有反击部队能够接近的道路。两侧地面起伏，法国步兵的接近同时受到较近阵地和坡后德军火力威胁。")},
    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 杜奥蒙外围 · 一九一六年十月二十四日\n\n炮火越过堡垒下方的坡面，反攻开始。德军自二月占着杜奥蒙，铁丝横在上坡路上。先头队伏于弹坑，等工兵把剪钳送到壕口。\n\n坡脊挡住了后面的枪位。携弹手贴着坑岸前送，军士沿两条接近路传下出发口令。电话线拖过积水，接线兵跪在泥里；连部等着第一声来自高处的回话。\n\n法军在这次反攻中收复杜奥蒙堡垒。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Outside Douaumont · Twenty-four October nineteen sixteen\n\nThe guns lift over the slope below the fort and the counteroffensive opens. German troops have held Douaumont since February. Wire crosses the uphill approaches. The leading men lie in shell holes while the sappers bring their cutters to the trench mouth.\n\nThe crest hides the guns behind it. Bearers follow the crater banks. Orders pass down both approaches. A telephone wire drags through water; the linesman kneels in the mud. Headquarters waits for the first answer from the heights.\n\nFrench forces recovered Fort Douaumont in this counteroffensive."), TEXT("On 24 October 1916, the French counteroffensive opens around Douaumont, north of Verdun. The fort has been in German hands since February. French artillery preparation precedes the attack across the surrounding heights, where months of bombardment have damaged the ground and the German defensive positions.\n\nThe company is on the outer slopes below the fort. Wire bars both uphill approaches, and the ridge hides part of the German line. Behind the nearer defences, an approach remains available for counterattacking troops. The German crest positions and the approaches behind them face French attacks from the lower slope.")},
    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 杜奥蒙外围 · 一九一六年十月二十四日"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Outside Douaumont · Twenty-four October nineteen sixteen"), TEXT("行军作战日志 · 杜奥蒙外围 · 一九一六年十月二十四日")},
