    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 卢沃蒙 · 一九一六年十二月\n\n鞋拔出泥时带起一声响，前队停在村道旁等候。法军又向凡尔登北面进攻，路堤与树林挡住邻班。离开路面的士兵陷得更深，只能扶着彼此回到硬地。\n\n铁丝横过坡面，携弹队从残留缺口挤进来。枪声在脊后响起，军士伏到路边观察。担架送过时众人贴住墙根，湿泥从伤员的衣角滴在石头上。\n\n凡尔登战役持续约三百日。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Louvemont · December nineteen sixteen\n\nBoots pull free of the mud with a sharp sound. The leading men wait beside the village road. The French advance north of Verdun has resumed, but trees and an embankment hide the next section. Men leaving the road sink deeper.\n\nWire crosses the slope. Bearers squeeze through a surviving gap as firing starts beyond the ridge. The NCO lies beside the track to observe. Men press against the wall for a passing stretcher; mud drips from its occupant's coat onto the stones.\n\nThe Battle of Verdun lasted about three hundred days."), TEXT("一九一六年十二月，法军在凡尔登北面再次反攻，向秋季作战收复的地段之外推进。卢沃蒙与胡椒丘附近，冬季泥泞和低能见度妨碍步兵行动。村道比两侧田地坚实，却处在德军火力能够监视的范围内。\n\n本连所在的地段介于村落入口与林间路堤之间，铁丝网分隔坡地，离开道路后，松软田地又使行军迟缓。坡后枪位难以观察，破损道路还承载着弹药运输和伤员回送。反攻沿着这样一条冬季战线展开。")},
    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 卢沃蒙 · 一九一六年十二月\n\n鞋拔出泥时带起一声响，前队停在村道旁等候。法军又向凡尔登北面进攻，路堤与树林挡住邻班。离开路面的士兵陷得更深，只能扶着彼此回到硬地。\n\n铁丝横过坡面，携弹队从残留缺口挤进来。枪声在脊后响起，军士伏到路边观察。担架送过时众人贴住墙根，湿泥从伤员的衣角滴在石头上。\n\n凡尔登战役持续约三百日。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Louvemont · December nineteen sixteen\n\nBoots pull free of the mud with a sharp sound. The leading men wait beside the village road. The French advance north of Verdun has resumed, but trees and an embankment hide the next section. Men leaving the road sink deeper.\n\nWire crosses the slope. Bearers squeeze through a surviving gap as firing starts beyond the ridge. The NCO lies beside the track to observe. Men press against the wall for a passing stretcher; mud drips from its occupant's coat onto the stones.\n\nThe Battle of Verdun lasted about three hundred days."), TEXT("In December 1916, the French renew their counteroffensive north of Verdun, extending the ground recovered during the autumn fighting. Around Louvemont and the Côte du Poivre, winter mud and poor visibility hinder the infantry. The village road is firmer than the neighbouring fields, but lies within German fields of fire.\n\nThe company operates between the village approaches and the wooded embankment. Wire divides this ground, while soft fields slow movement away from the road. Guns behind the slopes are difficult to observe. The attack develops across a winter front where damaged roads also carry supplies and returning wounded.")},
    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 卢沃蒙 · 一九一六年十二月"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Louvemont · December nineteen sixteen"), TEXT("行军作战日志 · 卢沃蒙 · 一九一六年十二月")},
