    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 拉马尔梅松 · 一九一七年十月二十三日\n\n重炮轰过的交通壕里满是碎土，工兵走在步兵旁边。进攻队来到贵妇小径的这段高地，坡上的铁丝还挂着断桩。军士沿壕角核对前队的位置。\n\n炮声向远处移去，枪组把器材送到转弯处。先头队试着看清脊后，视线却被胸墙挡住。工兵放下工具，伏着向铁丝接近，后面的人留下了够一副担架通过的空隙。\n\n法军在十月攻占拉马尔梅松一带。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · La Malmaison · Twenty-three October nineteen seventeen\n\nHeavy shells have filled the communication trench with loose earth. Sappers walk beside the infantry towards this stretch of the Chemin des Dames. Broken stakes still hold wire on the slope. The NCO checks the leading party at each traverse.\n\nThe guns lift farther away. A crew brings its equipment to the bend. Men try to see beyond the ridge, but the parapet blocks their view. A sapper crawls towards the wire; those behind leave space for a stretcher to pass.\n\nFrench forces captured the La Malmaison sector in October."), TEXT("一九一七年十月二十三日，法军向拉马尔梅松发起进攻。春季攻势失败后，这次行动集中于贵妇小径上一段较短的战线。重炮已连续轰击设防高地。\n\n本连沿炮击后的交通壕接近山脊。铁丝网和折线枪位仍守着坡地，工兵随步兵向前方工事推进。山脊之后，还有看不见的德军阵地。")},
    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 拉马尔梅松 · 一九一七年十月二十三日\n\n重炮轰过的交通壕里满是碎土，工兵走在步兵旁边。进攻队来到贵妇小径的这段高地，坡上的铁丝还挂着断桩。军士沿壕角核对前队的位置。\n\n炮声向远处移去，枪组把器材送到转弯处。先头队试着看清脊后，视线却被胸墙挡住。工兵放下工具，伏着向铁丝接近，后面的人留下了够一副担架通过的空隙。\n\n法军在十月攻占拉马尔梅松一带。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · La Malmaison · Twenty-three October nineteen seventeen\n\nHeavy shells have filled the communication trench with loose earth. Sappers walk beside the infantry towards this stretch of the Chemin des Dames. Broken stakes still hold wire on the slope. The NCO checks the leading party at each traverse.\n\nThe guns lift farther away. A crew brings its equipment to the bend. Men try to see beyond the ridge, but the parapet blocks their view. A sapper crawls towards the wire; those behind leave space for a stretcher to pass.\n\nFrench forces captured the La Malmaison sector in October."), TEXT("On 23 October 1917, French infantry attacks at La Malmaison. After the failed spring offensive, the new operation concentrates on a shorter front along the Chemin des Dames. Heavy artillery has battered the fortified heights.\n\nBelow the ridge, the company's approach trench turns through shelled ground. German wire and angular firing positions still defend the slope. Engineers move with the infantry towards the nearer works; further positions remain hidden beyond the crest.")},
    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 拉马尔梅松 · 一九一七年十月二十三日"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · La Malmaison · Twenty-three October nineteen seventeen"), TEXT("行军作战日志 · 拉马尔梅松 · 一九一七年十月二十三日")},
