    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 香槟 · 一九一八年七月十五日\n\n前哨回来的人从壕口钻入，带来德军进攻的消息。古罗的第四集团军守着纵深阵地，主防线还在后面。田野上的枪位被坡地隔开，电话里同时有人报告。\n\n两条交通壕通向后方，携弹手站在转角让出路。军士查过回来的人，再派联络兵去找邻哨。沟外地面被枪弹扫过，报信的人把帽子压低，重新向前走。\n\n德军七月进攻未能突破香槟防线。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Champagne · Fifteen July nineteen eighteen\n\nMen returning from the outposts enter the trench with news of the German attack. Gouraud's Fourth Army holds positions in depth, with the main line farther behind. Slopes separate the guns across the fields. Reports overlap on the telephone.\n\nTwo communication trenches lead back. A bearer stands aside at a traverse. The NCO checks the returning men and sends a runner towards the next post. Bullets cross the ground outside. The messenger lowers his cap and starts forward along the trench again.\n\nThe German July attack failed to break through in Champagne."), TEXT("一九一八年七月十五日，德军进攻沙隆东北的法国香槟阵线。古罗的第四集团军已组织纵深防御，前哨位于主阵地之前，分散在农田上的各处阵位依靠交通壕相连，前后并不都能互相看见。\n\n本连位于这套防御的外侧，两条壕沟从前哨地段通向后方，沟外地面暴露在火力之下。德军可能先压到外围，后侧才逐渐掌握攻击范围。主阵地仍在身后，报告与退回的人员都要经过前后之间的地段，受到那里交火的影响。")},
    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 香槟 · 一九一八年七月十五日\n\n前哨回来的人从壕口钻入，带来德军进攻的消息。古罗的第四集团军守着纵深阵地，主防线还在后面。田野上的枪位被坡地隔开，电话里同时有人报告。\n\n两条交通壕通向后方，携弹手站在转角让出路。军士查过回来的人，再派联络兵去找邻哨。沟外地面被枪弹扫过，报信的人把帽子压低，重新向前走。\n\n德军七月进攻未能突破香槟防线。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Champagne · Fifteen July nineteen eighteen\n\nMen returning from the outposts enter the trench with news of the German attack. Gouraud's Fourth Army holds positions in depth, with the main line farther behind. Slopes separate the guns across the fields. Reports overlap on the telephone.\n\nTwo communication trenches lead back. A bearer stands aside at a traverse. The NCO checks the returning men and sends a runner towards the next post. Bullets cross the ground outside. The messenger lowers his cap and starts forward along the trench again.\n\nThe German July attack failed to break through in Champagne."), TEXT("On 15 July 1918, German forces attack the French front in Champagne, northeast of Châlons. Gouraud's Fourth Army has organised its defence in depth. The outposts stand ahead of the main line, with communication trenches linking the separated positions across the farmland.\n\nThe company occupies the outer part of this defence. Two trenches run back from its outpost sector, while the intervening ground is exposed to fire. A German attack can reach the forward posts before its extent is clear farther back. The main positions remain behind them, separated by ground across which reports and withdrawing troops must pass.")},
    {TEXT("行军作战日志 · 香槟 · 一九一八年七月十五日"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF MARCHES AND OPERATIONS · Champagne · Fifteen July nineteen eighteen"), TEXT("行军作战日志 · 香槟 · 一九一八年七月十五日")},
