    {TEXT("军事行动日志 · 卢茨克 · 一九一六年六月四日\n\n接近壕尽头传来炮声，西南方面军开始进攻。奥匈军的铁丝已经看得清楚，两处缺口各有一条壕道相通。排长在壕角交代出发次序。\n\n第一道工事后面还有深壕，田野无遮无挡。前队压低枪口等待，携弹手把箱子递过泥水。担架队留在接近壕内，点名的人把尚未出发的各班又查了一遍。\n\n布鲁西洛夫攻势突破了奥匈军在卢茨克一带的防御。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF OPERATIONS · Lutsk · Four June nineteen sixteen\n\nThe guns sound beyond the head of the approach trench. The Southwestern Front has begun its attack. Austro-Hungarian wire is already visible, with a trench leading to each of the two gaps. The platoon commander gives the order of departure at the traverse.\n\nA deeper trench lies behind the first works; the fields between are bare. The leading men keep their muzzles low. Bearers pass boxes over the water. Stretcher parties wait in the approach trench as the remaining sections answer the roll again.\n\nBrusilov's offensive broke the Austro-Hungarian defences around Lutsk."), TEXT("一九一六年六月四日，俄国西南战线对奥匈阵地展开布鲁西洛夫攻势。卢茨克附近，预先准备的接近地使俄罗斯步兵靠近敌军壕沟。不同地段同时受到压力，奥匈防御面临的攻击并不集中于单一据点。\n\n本连位于卢茨克接近地，两条壕沟分别通向铁丝网中的不同缺口。奥匈阵线在较近工事后面仍有纵深壕沟，阵地之间的田野暴露在观察范围内。接近壕输送俄军人员，前方地面则由敌军较近与较深的阵位共同监视。")},
    {TEXT("军事行动日志 · 卢茨克 · 一九一六年六月四日\n\n接近壕尽头传来炮声，西南方面军开始进攻。奥匈军的铁丝已经看得清楚，两处缺口各有一条壕道相通。排长在壕角交代出发次序。\n\n第一道工事后面还有深壕，田野无遮无挡。前队压低枪口等待，携弹手把箱子递过泥水。担架队留在接近壕内，点名的人把尚未出发的各班又查了一遍。\n\n布鲁西洛夫攻势突破了奥匈军在卢茨克一带的防御。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF OPERATIONS · Lutsk · Four June nineteen sixteen\n\nThe guns sound beyond the head of the approach trench. The Southwestern Front has begun its attack. Austro-Hungarian wire is already visible, with a trench leading to each of the two gaps. The platoon commander gives the order of departure at the traverse.\n\nA deeper trench lies behind the first works; the fields between are bare. The leading men keep their muzzles low. Bearers pass boxes over the water. Stretcher parties wait in the approach trench as the remaining sections answer the roll again.\n\nBrusilov's offensive broke the Austro-Hungarian defences around Lutsk."), TEXT("On 4 June 1916, the Russian Southwestern Front opens the Brusilov offensive against Austro-Hungarian positions. Around Lutsk, prepared approaches bring Russian infantry close to the enemy trenches. Pressure is applied along several parts of the front, making the defence respond beyond a single threatened position.\n\nThe company is in the Lutsk approaches, where two trenches lead towards separate gaps in the wire. The Austro-Hungarian line extends into a deeper trench behind the nearer works. Fields between the positions are exposed to observation, while the approach trenches carry Russian troops towards the first defensive belt.")},
    {TEXT("军事行动日志 · 卢茨克 · 一九一六年六月四日\n\n接近壕尽头传来炮声，西南方面军开始进攻。奥匈军的铁丝已经看得清楚，两处缺口各有一条壕道相通。排长在壕角交代出发次序。\n\n第一道工事后面还有深壕，田野无遮无挡。前队压低枪口等待，携弹手把箱子递过泥水。担架队留在接近壕内，点名的人把尚未出发的各班又查了一遍。\n\n布鲁西洛夫攻势突破了奥匈军在卢茨克一带的防御。"), TEXT("JOURNAL OF OPERATIONS · Lutsk · Four June nineteen sixteen\n\nThe guns sound beyond the head of the approach trench. The Southwestern Front has begun its attack. Austro-Hungarian wire is already visible, with a trench leading to each of the two gaps. The platoon commander gives the order of departure at the traverse.\n\nA deeper trench lies behind the first works; the fields between are bare. The leading men keep their muzzles low. Bearers pass boxes over the water. Stretcher parties wait in the approach trench as the remaining sections answer the roll again.\n\nBrusilov's offensive broke the Austro-Hungarian defences around Lutsk."), TEXT("JOURNAL OF OPERATIONS · Lutsk · Four June nineteen sixteen\n\nThe guns sound beyond the head of the approach trench. The Southwestern Front has begun its attack. Austro-Hungarian wire is already visible, with a trench leading to each of the two gaps. The platoon commander gives the order of departure at the traverse.\n\nA deeper trench lies behind the first works; the fields between are bare. The leading men keep their muzzles low. Bearers pass boxes over the water. Stretcher parties wait in the approach trench as the remaining sections answer the roll again.\n\nBrusilov’s offensive broke the Austro-Hungarian defences around Lutsk.")},
